  "notes": "Mill Creek Residential: millcreekplaces.com/portfolio/ is a JS-driven search widget that returns no server-rendered results, so it could not be used directly. Instead pulled millcreekplaces.com/community-sitemap.xml (via curl) to enumerate all ~140 community slugs nationwide, then fetched each Colorado-looking candidate page individually to confirm address/state and pull each community's own marketing domain from the 'View Community' button. Found 7 Modera-branded CO communities (all Denver) plus 1 Amavi-branded (Thornton) build-to-rent townhome community. Ruled out modera-douglas-station (Miami, FL) and modera-ridgeline (McKinney, TX) despite plausible-sounding names. Amavi Thornton has no dedicated marketing domain yet (still in lease-up/pre-opening per Jan 2026 groundbreaking release) - marketing_url null.\n\nWood Partners: woodpartners.com/where-we-live/ 404'd; used woodpartners.com/properties/ (Property Archive) instead, which listed 9 CO properties (site mislabeled all of them 'Denver' as a region header - actual cities per each property's own page are Longmont, Superior, Aurora, Lakewood x3, and Denver x2). Individual property pages on woodpartners.com rarely link to a branded marketing site; only Alta Mile High, Alta Sloan's Lake, Alta SoBo Station, and The Grove at City Center have confirmed dedicated marketing domains found via search. Altera Longmont, Alta Flatirons, and Alta Metro Center are new/under-construction with no leasing site yet. Alta Pinehurst's known domain (altapinehurst.com) no longer resolves (DNS failure) and third-party listings suggest it may now be rebranded/managed as 'Windsor at Pinehurst' by Windsor Communities - kept on list per Wood Partners' own current portfolio page but marketing_url set null pending verification. Alta Green Mountain shows signs of a 2025 sale (NorthMarq transaction record, Yelp listing marked closed) but still appears on Wood Partners' own portfolio page as of this search, so it is included with a caution note and no marketing_url found. Note: Alta Piney Creek/Alta Addison (Aurora) turned up in general search but is NOT on Wood Partners' current /properties/ page and is now Greystar-managed - excluded as no longer a Wood Partners property.\n\nAlliance Residential (Broadstone): allresco.com has NO public searchable communities/portfolio page - checked homepage nav, /segments/, /communities/ (404), /portfolio/ (404). Alliance is a merchant developer that routinely sells stabilized assets (confirmed recent dispositions: Broadstone Kendrick, Broadstone Sterling Ranch $121M sale to Coit Financial Group, Highlands32, Dylan all sold/disposed; Broadstone Lowry and Broadstone New Territory (Colorado Springs) now appear managed by Greystar and BH Management respectively, not Alliance). Because there is no operator portfolio page to verify against, this section is assembled from press coverage and should be treated as LOWER CONFIDENCE / possibly stale - included per completeness goal but flagged. Included only communities with no confirmed sale/rebrand found: Broadstone Vesta, Broadstone Montane, Broadstone on 9th, Broadstone Gardens at Cherry Creek. Excluded confirmed-sold/rebranded ones (Kendrick, Sterling Ranch, Highlands32, Dylan, Lowry, New Territory).\n\nSimpson Property Group: simpsonpropertygroup.com/apartment-search rendered a full nationwide list server-side; cross-checked against simpsonpropertygroup.com/cities/denver and /cities/affordable-denver-apartments. Found 9 CO communities, all in the Denver metro (Denver, Aurora, Parker, Thornton). None of the CO properties have their own branded domain - all link to pages on simpsonpropertygroup.com itself, so own_domain is false for all nine (own_domain:false, not vendor-hosted).\n\nCardinal Group Management: cardinalgroup.com/portfolio/ rendered server-side with a clean state-by-state table including direct marketing-site links for each property, including a Colorado-highlighted section - this was the cleanest, most reliable source of the five operators. Found 12 CO multifamily/BTR properties (Denver, Colorado Springs, Aurora x2, Wheat Ridge, Gypsum, Eagle x2, Evans, Boulder, Erie). BB Living Colliers Hill (Erie) had no website listed (marketing_url null). No CO student-housing properties were listed for Cardinal (their CO book is multifamily/BTR).\n\nNo vendor-hosted (securecafe/rentcafe/appfolio/etc.) domains were fetched or included per the hard rules; a couple of search results surfaced rentcafe.com listings for some properties but those were not used as the marketing_url.",
